{#- The decision as an agent reads it back: the verdict, then each comment
    on the element it hangs on, by kind: what to change, what was asked,
    what to keep. A selector finds the element in the document as it was
    reviewed, and its text finds it again if the selector has moved. The
    head (title, origin, who decided, the note to the agent) is printed by
    the app before this. -#}
{%- macro comment(c) -%}
- `{{ c.selector }}`{% if c.snippet %} “{{ c.snippet }}”{% endif %}: {{ c.text }}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- set changes = items | selectattr("kind", "equalto", "change") | list -%}
{%- set questions = items | selectattr("kind", "equalto", "question") | list -%}
{%- set keep = items | selectattr("kind", "equalto", "praise") | list -%}
Verdict: {{ "approved" if data.verdict == "approve" else "revise" }}
{%- if changes %}

## Change
{% for c in changes %}
{{ comment(c) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if questions %}

## Questions
{% for c in questions %}
{{ comment(c) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if keep %}

## Keep
{% for c in keep %}
{{ comment(c) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
